# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Order matters: the FIRST matching rule wins, and Cloudflare does not chain
# redirects — every rule points at its FINAL URL.
#
# Topology (D-W1, Task 8): English is canonical at the root; Spanish lives at
# /es. Consequences for previously published URLs:
#   - Old /en/... URLs (English used to live there) → the same path at root.
#   - Old root URLs served Spanish; their route families are retired, so they
#     301 to the closest surviving surface, refined per-task as Cabuya pages
#     land.
#
# Task 23 removed the /developers rule, Task 30 removed /governance, /conduct
# and /contributing, and /about went the same way when the origin page landed:
# those routes are now live English pages, and a redirect to the Spanish home
# would have shadowed them. `redirects:check` caught every one, which is what a
# shadow check is for — a rule that hides a page is invisible in a diff and
# total in production.
#
# The retired ones point at the surviving surface: /conduct and /contributing
# are the community files, which now live at /join and on GitHub.
# An old inbound link that expected Spanish content there lands on the English
# portal with the language switcher one click away — which is the topology
# working as designed, not a regression. Redirecting it to /es/ instead would
# have sent a reader looking for developer documentation to the home page.

# --- Retired routes (old Spanish root URLs) → closest surface --------------
/how-it-works                /es/    301
/transparency                /es/    301
/emergencies                 /es/    301
/leaders                     /es/    301
/partners                    /es/    301
/ecosystem                   /es/    301
/privacy                     /es/    301
/contact                     /es/    301
/movement                    /es/    301
/movement/*                  /es/    301
/channels                    /es/    301
/conduct                     /join   301
/contributing                /join   301
/community                   /es/    301
/blog                        /es/    301
/blog/*                      /es/    301
/rss.xml                     /es/    301

# --- Retired API endpoints -------------------------------------------------
/api/posts.json              /    301
/api/posts-en.json           /    301
/api/posts-es.json           /    301
/api/series/*                /    301
/api/timeline/*              /    301

# --- Old English URLs: /en moved to the root -------------------------------
# The route families are retired, so everything funnels to the new root.
/en                          /    301
/en/*                        /    301
